{"id":"word:hebrew:H6299","type":"word","title":"פָּדָה","subtitle":"H6299 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to sever , i.e. ransom ; generally to release , preserve","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to פָּדָה (H6299) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 59 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"פָּדָה (pâdâh) means to sever , i.e. ransom ; generally to release , preserve First listed occurrence: 1Chr 17 21."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"פָּדָה","transliteration":"pâdâh","pronunciation":"paw-daw'","strong":"H6299","lemmaId":"hebrew:H6299","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["תִפְדֶּ֖ה","יִפְדֶּ֣ה","פָּדָ֥ה","פָּדִ֨יתָ֙","תִּפְדֶּ֣ה"],"morphs":[["HVqi2ms",10],["HVqp2ms",7],["HVqp3ms",6],["HC/Vqw3ms/Sp2ms",3],["HVqv2ms/Sp1cs",3],["HVqi3ms",3],["HR/Vqc",2],["HVqi1cs/Sp3mp",2],["HC/Vqsmpc",2],["HVqa",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"to sever , i.e. ransom ; generally to release , preserve","usage":"× at all, deliver, × by any means, ransom, (that are to be, let be) redeem(-ed), rescue, × surely.","full":"H6299. padah מָּדָה verb ransom (Late Hebrew in derivatives; Phoenician in proper name; Assyrian padû , id. , Arabic ; Ethiopic ; Minaean פדית redeemed or purchased land Mordt Beitr. 23 ); — Qal Perfect 3masculine singular מָּדָה Lev 27:27 +; suffix מָּֽדְךָ Job 5:20 ; 2 masculine singular מָּדִיתָ Deut 9:26 +, etc.; Imperfect יִפְדֶּה Psa 49:8 +, etc.; Imperative מְּדֵה 25:22 ; suffix מְּדֵנִי 26:11 3 t.; Infinitive absolute מָּדֹה Num 18:15 ; Psa 49:8 ; construct לִפְדּוֺת 2Sam 7:23 = 1Chr 17:2 ; Participle active מּוֺדֶה Psalm 34:23; suffix מֹּדְךָ Deut 13:6 ; passive plural construct מְּדוּיֵּי Isa 35:10 ; 51:11 ; Num 3:49 ; also absolute מְּדוּיִם 3:51 (Qr; Kt פדים ), construct מְּדוּיֵי 3:46 ; suffix מְּדוּיָו 18:16 (all noun abstract according to Di Kö ii. 1, 138 , see מִּדְיֹם מְּדוּיִם, below); — ransom: 1 for an assessed price Exod 13:13 , 15 ; 34:20 (J), Lev 27:27 ; Num 3:46 , 48 , 49 , 51 ; 18:15-16 , 17 (P). 2 from violence and death 1Sam 14:45 ; Job 6:23 ; Psa 49:8 . 3 God subject (underlying thought of payment): a. from Egypt, with עֲבָדִים מִבֵּית מִן, Deut 7:8 ; 13:6 ; Micah 6:4 ; מִנִּיצָֿר Psa 78:42 ; ממצרים 2Sam 7:23 (but strike out מָּדִיתָ Gei Urschr. 288 We Dr and others) = 1Chr 17:21 ; מִשָּׁם Deut 24:18 ; absolute 9:26 ; 15:15 ; 21:8 ; Neh 1:10 . b. from exile , Jer 31:11 ; Zech 10:8 ; י ׳מְּדוּיֵּי יְשֻׁבוּן Isa 35:10 = 51:11 . c. in General Hosea 7:13 ; צָרוֺתָיו מִכֹּל Psa 25:22 ; עֲוֺנוֺתָיו מִכֹּל 130:8 . d. with accusative individual Psa 26:11 ; 31:6 ; Psalm 44:27; 69:19 ; Abraham Isa 29:22 ; נפשׁ ׳פ Psalm 34:23; Psa 71:23 ; + צרה מכל 2Sam 4:9 ; 1Kin 1:29 ; בַּשָּׁ֑חַת מֵעֲבֹר Job 33:28 ; מִקְּרָבלִֿי Psa 55:19 ; מִמָּוֶת Job 5:20 ; שׁאול מיד Psa 49:16 ; Hosea 13:14 ; אָדָם מֵעשֶׁק Psa 119:134 ; עָרִיצִים מִכַּף Jer 15:21 . Niph`al Perfect 3feminine singular (+ Hoph`al Infinitive absolute ) נִפְדָּ֑תָה לֹא הָפְדֵּה Lev 19:20 she hath not been at all ransomed (from bondage); Imperfect יִמָּדֶה 27:29 (from ban); 3 feminine singular תִּמָּדֶ֑ה בְּמִשְׁמָּט צִיּוֺן Isa 1:27 . Hiph`il Perfect 3masculine singular suffix וְהֶפְדָּהּ Exod 21:8 he shall let her be ransomed . Hiph`il Infinitive absolute see Niph`al","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 17 21","keyReferences":["1Chr 17 21","1Chr 17 21","1Kgs 1 29","1Sam 14 45","2Sam 4 9","2Sam 7 23","2Sam 7 23","Deut 7 8"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":59,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 17 21","book":"1Chr","chapter":17,"verse":21,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לִ/פְדּ֧וֹת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Vqc"},{"reference":"1Chr 17 21","book":"1Chr","chapter":17,"verse":21,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"פָּדִ֥יתָ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqp2ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 1 29","bo